He declined to comment on the incident, which could have led to security breaches.
Without the permission of the card processing company and the security staff, the bank no longer receives this information.
Additional security measures are being planned for ACLEDA Bank customers, including data, codes and credentials such as grouping or confidentiality.
While the new system does not completely stop fraud, we can do everything we can to protect our customers.
ACLEDA Bank created more than one million accounts as of November 30 and announced a total asset value of US $ 2 billion in the third quarter of 2013.
Senior government officials have again called on local enterprises to improve quality and increase productivity to compete with the influx of foreign products as ASEAN economic integration approaches in 2015.
The call was made at a national workshop on modern food safety management systems yesterday in Phnom Penh.
The entry of the ASEAN Economic Community in 2015 means that goods from all 10 ASEAN countries will be allowed to cross the border duty-free.
Minister of Industry, Mines and Energy Cham Prasidh saw it as an opportunity, but questioned whether Cambodian goods were ready for export at a time when domestic production was still limited in both quality and standards.
According to Cham Prasidh, small and medium enterprises account for about 99 percent of the total number of enterprises and industries in the country, most of which are still limited in production capacity.
The second is the investment capital to improve the current situation in accordance with the standards, such as improving the reconstruction of the building, covering the room, installing glass and installing some materials.
It requires capital investment and, ultimately, a shortage of skilled suppliers to the company because there are fewer professionals than the number of enterprises.
In order to export food products, enterprises or manufacturers need a certificate stating that the exported goods will not endanger the health of consumers.
Cham Prasidh says local entrepreneurs must be prepared to stand in the common market of ASEAN.
There are currently a total of 505,134 small and medium enterprises in Cambodia.
More illegal pawn shops
The number of pawn shops in Cambodia has risen to hundreds, most concentrated in major cities, but a large number of pawnshops do not have proper business licenses.
According to business people in the industry.
According to some well-licensed pawn shop owners in Phnom Penh, the proliferation of unlicensed pawn shops is making it difficult for legal pawnshops and users.
So Khun, owner of SYT Mobile Pawnshop, a legal pawn shop that accepts mortgages on cars, motorcycles and other movable items, said the number of pawn shops in Phnom Penh had risen sharply to just hundreds. Only 10 percent of large pawnshops with valid operating licenses from the Ministry of Economy and Finance.
He said that many illegal pawnshops do not have many requirements when customers place collateral, and some accept collateral from criminals, while some pawn shops accept collateral from students or undocumented property. This makes the recipient more vulnerable and damages the reputation of the legitimate pawn shop.
This is a challenge that we are demanding the Ministry to help.
According to a proclamation from the Ministry of Economy and Finance, in order to obtain a pawn shop operation license, business owners must have a minimum capital of 200 million riels and must deposit 10 percent to the ministry.
The company pays an annual fee of $ 250 and distributes 15 percent of its profits to renew its license annually.
This problem not only affects the company, but it also makes it very difficult for customers because users of this service may have to pay higher interest than the market to get the money needed in exchange for that. Illegal pawnshops do not require many conditions.
Mey Van, director general of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, confirmed to the Post yesterday that the ministry was trying to legalize the business, so that all unlicensed pawnshops were being set up. Under the administrative action of the Ministry.
So far, he said, he has not received any new information from the company.
