Last year, CEDAC exported 150 tonnes of rice.
The contract to buy rice from farmers will ensure the quality and quantity of rice produced.
We have also been in contact with the farming community.
Yang Saing Koma, President of CEDAC, said that most of the challenges faced by farmers were the high volatility of market prices, which put farmers at high risk due to a lack of information on the amount of demand and global rice market prices. Farmers can not determine the price and quantity of production according to market demand.
