Farmers need to make a contract.
Farmer Prak Nai hopes that the contract to supply rice to rice mills will help reduce the risk of farmers borrowing for agriculture.
Nim Kuon, a farmer in Thmor Koul district's Chrey commune, used to expect his rice crop to sell well after the floods, but was disappointed when brokers lowered prices.
He is interested in signing a contract with the mill, but says he is reluctant because he is not sure he can get a fair price for the rice.
The government issued a sub-decree to implement agricultural product contracts in 2011.
Mr. Yang Saing Koma said that Cambodia has little experience in implementing agricultural product contracts, but he stressed that it is important and hoped that in the future, the implementation of agricultural contracts in Cambodia will be more. More in agriculture.
