Four countries together to increase tourist attraction
Kampot: Four ASEAN countries - Cambodia, Laos, Myanmar and Vietnam - CLMV plans to implement joint tourism symbols to promote the tourism potential of the four countries to attract and increase the number of tourists.
The CLMV Tourism Symbol is scheduled to be launched in February 2014, a decision to support the CLMV tourism cooperation direction under the theme of four countries, one destination to attract 25 million international tourists per year in 2015. .
Speaking at a press conference at the second CLMV Ministerial Meeting on Tourism last weekend at the Thansur Bokor resort in Kampot province, Tith Chantha, secretary of state at the Ministry of Tourism, said the four countries had decided to establish and implement tourism symbols. Together to promote the tourism potential of CLMV countries and to attract more tourists to visit these four countries.
