Cambodia's service sector faces challenges
Phnom Penh: A new report from the Asian Development Bank (ADB) shows that Cambodia has not yet been able to take full advantage of the development of the service sector, despite the fact that the sector is gaining some momentum due to many obstacles Still can not be resolved.
In a presentation yesterday on the release of a report entitled “Developing the Services Sector as a Growth Driver for Asia,” ADB Vice President for Cambodia Peter Brimble said that many developing countries, including Cambodia, are embracing There has been growth in the service sector, but the momentum of this growth is not yet very effective and low productivity.
According to the ADB report, the services sector continues to struggle due to a lack of rural transport infrastructure, high electricity costs, high logistics and transportation costs, as well as implementation-related challenges. Laws and regulations.
Lack of skilled labor and institutional capacity also remains an obstacle.
In Cambodia, the tourism industry is a key component of the growth of the service sector, and it is experiencing significant growth.
