This is according to Ms. Chey Siyat, the head of the rice farming community in Damnak Kantuot commune in Kampong Trach district, Kampot province.
For Chey Siyat, who graduated from sixth grade, this opportunity is a great way for people to truly understand how to relate to someone's real life.
Ms. Chey Siyat noted that climate change is a growing concern recently, even among non-agricultural communities, and has become a challenge for women farmers, leading to declining agricultural yields. Low.
