Hong Heap stops repairing unlicensed cars
Phnom Penh: Hong Heap, the exclusive distributor of Mercedes-Benz cars in Cambodia, announced yesterday that it will stop providing repair and replacement services for Mercedes-Benz vehicles purchased by consumers from unlicensed car dealerships in Germany. .
Khun Chantha, Marketing Manager for Mercedes in Cambodia, said the company would stop offering the service from 2013 Mercedes-Benz to encourage customers to turn away from non-importing vehicles. To be right and to be a part of increasing the company's car sales in the market.
Currently, the sales volume of Mercedes-Benz vehicles in the market is half that between Hong Heap and unlicensed dealers.
