Chanthy, president of the Cambodian Economic Association, also agreed that investors were unlikely to co-operate with the CNRP, but the slight disturbance mentioned by Sam Rainsy could lead investors to invest in Cambodia. By careful consideration.
A boycott requires long-term pressure to be effective.
The political situation in Cambodia is very different compared to the political situation in South Africa at the time of the secession, but it took decades for the nationwide economic boycott to be effective in order to change the system. This racist politics.
The CNRP is confident of organizing its simultaneous one-day mass demonstrations across the country.
Son Chhay, the CNRP's parliamentary group leader, said it was not just young people who supported the campaign, but also shopkeepers, market vendors, motodup drivers, tuk-tuk drivers and people from all walks of life.
Ms. Chanthy said the demonstrations would not last long as people had to earn money to support their families.
Kong Athit, vice president of CCAWDU, expects 40 to 50 percent of the 80,000 factory workers to join the strike.
He said phased strategies, such as long-term demonstrations, could still be effective, and he hoped the two political parties could find common ground in the face of pressure.
Shopping service reaches the suburbs
Phnom Penh: Shopping malls are beginning to expand their operations from the city center to the suburbs of Phnom Penh, as demand for shopping services is growing and the size of the city is growing.
In fact, DFI Lucky Private Investment, which invested in Lucky Supermarkets last weekend, opened three more Lucky Three markets on the same day, all located on the outskirts of Phnom Penh, amid growing demand for supermarket services in both areas. That is even stronger.
Rich Chad Sear, CEO of DFI Lucky Private, told the Post that more and more people living on the outskirts of Phnom Penh are in need of shopping malls and are traveling to Phnom Penh to shop.
Therefore, seeing this, the company decided to include the downtown area around Phnom Penh into the project to expand the investment location and start operating from now on.
One is in Stung Meanchey Thmey Market and the other is in the southern part of Phnom Penh along National Road 21, about 500 meters from the Takhmao roundabout.
According to Richards, the investment capital of each Lucky supermarket is around $ 700,000, which includes the construction of buildings to run the market and the import of goods for sale.
The presence of these three additional supermarkets makes Lucky Supermarket a total of 11 branches, of which Siem Reap has one branch.
Suy Saki Hiroshi, an economist at the Business Research Institute of Cambodia, said the living conditions of people in both Phnom Penh and its suburbs had improved and that the rising middle-income population was driving There is a growing shopping industry in Cambodia.
However, Suy Saki said it had not yet become a serious threat to businesses in the regular market.
