The training was inaugurated yesterday in Phnom Penh.
This is the first international banking specialist training course in Cambodia that IBBM has partnered with the Banking Institute of Cambodia.
The Cambodian Banking Skills Training Institute was established by the Banking Association of Cambodia in 2004.
Therefore, it is imperative that everything we teach will benefit bankers to put it into practice in the workplace and can contribute to increasing productivity at the institutions they serve.
In this collaboration, IBBM will help prepare lessons, study schedules, documentation and other methods for the Banking Training Institute in Cambodia to bring this training to a standard level.
According to the IBBM representative, in order to receive a Certificate of Specialization from a Banker, all students must go through three major levels of training, each of which is divided into three sections for a total of nine courses.
The first level, which consists of three courses, costs about $ 750, and this price gradually increases as the level of education rises.
Eligible students are those who are currently working in banking and microfinance institutions with extensive experience in the field.
