Family business achieves great success
Superstitious influences in the business community have made 103 names a trademark of Li Zhouyi's business, which turned from a family craft business more than 20 years ago into a major trading company.
The business was started in 1989 when Li Chheng, Zhou Yi's father, rented a house around Orussey Market, 103, to run a glass cabinet business.
Mr. Ly Chheng started his business with a capital of almost 1 gram of gold and decided to name the craft 103.
Ms. Zhou Yi claimed:
So my father decided to use the number 103 to represent the name of his craft, which refers to the long-term prosperity of the business.
This belief was also very influential and contributed to encouraging Zhou Yi's family members to look at her father's business opportunities full of optimism.
Family solidarity, creative perseverance from the next generation have sustained the dreams and beliefs of Ly Chheng, who was deported to Cambodia from an area of China with poor living conditions.
More than a decade after 1989, in 2002, Ly Chheng's 103 Craft was transformed into a medium-sized commercial company called 103 New Products, a venture capital venture. All of which received expertise in this production from Mr. Ly Chheng.
Today, 103 New Products, located near the Chamkarmon traffic light, has offices for more than 70 employees, a separate factory with more than 100 employees, and a showroom with a wide range of furniture products.
At last week's Real Estate Expo, she also showcased her products.
Zhou Yi, who is now the Deputy General Manager of New Productions, said the company, which is now transforming from a family craft, has a wide range of home decor products, such as wallpaper, cabinets and cabinets. Glass in many other pieces of furniture made of cast iron.
As the housing sector, which is an important part of driving Cambodia's economic growth, continues to grow, the company's business operations continue to move forward.
The changing living conditions of the people in the city, combined with the large number of young families in need of housing, also contributed significantly to the strength of 103 New Products.
Ms. Zhou Yi claims that many customers come to buy products from the company after they have already bought a house and want to decorate the house to be more beautiful.
The company's target customers are middle-income and affluent families.
Zhou Yi and her brother, who specialize in factory production, have completed ninth grade in Chinese, so almost all of their knowledge in the field of aid is gained from practical business experience. .
The shadow of a father's past poverty has faded from the family for years.
The lessons of her father's life made Zhou Yi unforgettable, overcoming obstacles through perseverance and uniting forces to make progress to this day.
