Sathapana signs $ 15 million loan
Phnom Penh: Sathapana Microfinance Limited has signed a $ 15 million loan from German microfinance institution DEG to supplement its $ 143 million loan.
The next $ 15 million loan will focus on small and medium enterprises in Cambodia, with a one-year extension of up to one year.
This is according to the confirmation of the CEO of Sathapana.
Bun Mony, CEO of Sathapana Microfinance Institution, said the $ 15 million loan had a term of seven years, with an annual interest rate of between 6 and 6.3 percent, and that the money would support expansion. Services to small and medium businesses in the form of financing longer than 36 months to 48 months.
The microfinance institution also received $ 70 million in deposits from 54,334 senders over the same period nationwide with 101 executive offices.
Last year, DEG also provided a $ 15 million loan to PRASAC Microfinance to provide a wider range of financial services to small and medium enterprises.
We will add financing to other microfinance institutions in the future.
Mr. Bun Mony said that so far, SATHAPANA has more than 10 partners from different countries, including the United States, Switzerland, the Netherlands, Belgium, Luxembourg, Peru, France and Germany, and SATHAPANA holds a joint venture with Bank of Japan Maruhan, which owns 95% of the total capital. .
