Chuon Kol, deputy general manager of Men Sarun, a local noodle company, told the Post on Sunday that his company had increased production by about 40 per cent from 10,000 cases in the past. 14,000 cases per month.
He said the oversupply was due to a number of factors, including the current political situation, which has left people fearful after the election, and that Cambodia would later face floods that would require the distribution of noodles.
I told my seller not to raise the price at that time.
If we do this, it seems to kill our people.
