Kep: Officials at the Kep provincial tourism department expect at least 200,000 tourists and passengers to attend the Sea Festival by the end of the year.
The Sea Festival was interrupted a year ago last year as Cambodians mourn the death of the former King Father in October 2012.
The government organized the first Sea Festival in Sihanoukville, which drew tens of thousands of people, with an estimated 50,000 on the first day alone.
Som Chenda, director of the Kep provincial tourism department, said the sea festival, which will be held in Kep this year, would not be affected.
The government has decided to hold the festival on December 7 and 8 this year.
He added that the Sea Festival will be held at the same time as Cambodia celebrates the Clean Beach Convention at the Bokor Paradise Resort, which is also attended by members of the Clean Beach Club in the world.
Tourism Minister Thong Khon said in May that the General Assembly would be attended by officials from around the world.
He added that so far, the beaches that have become members of the world's most beautiful beaches are 39 in 30 countries around the world.
Cambodia Beach was officially recognized as a member of the World's Most Beautiful Beach Club on May 26, 2011.
