Phnom Penh: The latest biennial report assessing working conditions in Cambodia's garment factories of the International Labor Organization (ILO) BFC's Better Factories program shows that the situation related to the safety of Cambodian garment workers One step back since 2011.
While the BFC noted some improvements in workers' pay rights from earlier reports, concerns about factory inspections were continuing without compliance with safety and health, fire safety and child labor laws.
