He added that the Ministry of Commerce was trying to raise funds so that more products could be registered.
However, Ke Mony, deputy secretary general of the Khmer Silk Village Association, which has about 700 members, warned that the government should not rush into a decision to include Khmer silk in the GI, as regional imbalances are likely to occur. With production focused on a single area.
He said he would like to see capacity building across Cambodia, which produces only one tonne of silk a year and imports more than 30 tonnes.
The specification of the features is from the production method and the state of agriculture in the geographical area, which ensures the quality of the customers and allows them to monitor the product from the supermarket to the palm tree and pepper cultivation. Which they harvest.
The aim is through GI to expand the export market, with consumers paying higher prices for this unique quality.
Ministry of Economy delays tax collection
Phnom Penh: The Ministry of Economy and Finance has postponed the payment of taxes on all means of transportation and vehicles until the end of August.
A statement from the Ministry of Economy said that the delay was due to the busy schedule of voters, so the collection of taxes on all means of transportation would be postponed until August 31, 2013.
The tax unit will start implementing the fines from September 1, 2013, according to the statement.
